  "query_preview": "../ Saturday to Wednesday / Ridge aloft over the\neastern gulf and panhandle shifts east into British Columbia\nSunday chased by a short wave riding along the ridge axis and\npushing it along, while an upper low moves east over the Bering \nSea to near St. Lawrence Island. After Tuesday or so as model \nsolutions start having larger differences on where the short \nwaves are moving from south of the eastern Aleutians to the \nwestern gulf. A slightly stronger trough Tuesday has a better \nagreement over the central Aleutians, that looks like it will be \nswinging a low into the southeast Bering or the far western gulf \non the Tue/Wed time frame. \n\nSo what does this mean weather wise for Southeast... A break of\nnice weather through Saturday, as a front moves in from the west\nwith Moderate to heavy rain for the NE gulf coast, and gusty winds\nas the front moves through the area. Post frontal showers Monday\nto Tuesday. A trailing surface low possibility running into the\nsouthern panhandle late part of Wednesday.",
